</section>


<section><title>Video review questions</title>

  <ol>
  <li>
    <problem><title>Doubling time</title>

      <setup>
        <selectFromSequence name="a" from="1.1" to="4" step="0.1" />
        <number name="doublingTime">log(2)/log($a)</number>
      </setup>

      <p>If the population size <m>p_t</m> is growing according to <m>p_t = $a^t</m>, what is the doubling time of the population? <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" name="ans">$doublingTime</answer></p> 
      <p>(If rounding, include at least 4 digits in your response.)
      </p>

  <hint hide="$ans.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ans.creditAchieved = 1 or $ans.numSubmissions >= 5">
  <p>If a population is growing exponentially according to <m>p_t = a^t</m>, the doubling time is <m>t=\frac{\ln(2)}{\ln(a)}</m>.  In this example, <m>a=$a</m>.
  </p>
  </hint>
  
  <hint hide="$ans.numSubmissions &lt; 5 or $ans.creditAchieved = 1">
<p>If a population is growing exponentially according to <m>p_t = $a^t</m>, the doubling time is <m>t=\frac{\ln(2)}{\ln($a)} \approx <number displayDigits="4" extend="$doublingTime" /></m>.
</p>
</hint>


<solution>
<p>If a population is growing exponentially according to <m>p_t = $a^t</m>, the doubling time is <m>t=\frac{\ln(2)}{\ln($a)} \approx <number displayDigits="4" extend="$doublingTime" /></m>.
</p>

</solution>
      
    </problem>
  </li>
  <li>
    <problem><title>Half life</title>
      <setup>
        <selectFromSequence name="selectFromSequence" from="0.1" to="0.9" step="0.1" />
        <number name="halfLife">log(1/2)/log($selectFromSequence[1])</number>
      </setup>
      <p>If the population size <m>p_t</m> is shrinking according to <m>p_t = $selectFromSequence[1]^t</m>, what is the half life of the population? <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" name="ans">$halfLife</answer> 
      </p>
      <p>(If rounding, include at least 4 digits in your response.)
      </p>


  <hint hide="$ans.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ans.creditAchieved = 1 or $ans.numSubmissions >= 5">
  <p>If a population is shrinking according to <m>p_t = a^t</m>, the half life is <m>t=\frac{\ln(1/2)}{\ln(a)}</m>.  In this example, <m>a=$selectFromSequence[1]</m>.
  </p>
  </hint>
  
  <hint hide="$ans.numSubmissions &lt; 5 or $ans.creditAchieved = 1">
<p>If a population is shrinking according to <m>p_t = $selectFromSequence[1]^t</m>, the half life is <m>t=\frac{\ln(1/2)}{\ln($selectFromSequence[1])} \approx <number displayDigits="4" extend="$halfLife" /></m>.
</p>
</hint>


<solution>
<p>If a population is shrinking according to <m>p_t = $selectFromSequence[1]^t</m>, the half life is <m>t=\frac{\ln(1/2)}{\ln($selectFromSequence[1])} \approx <number displayDigits="4" extend="$halfLife" /></m>.
</p>

</solution>

      
    </problem>
  </li>

  </ol>

</section>
